# Month-End Period vs FY banner

## Bug (learned)

Reports Income Statement period can be **FY 01/07/2025–30/06/2026**.  
`viewPeriodId = firstMonthPeriodId(FY)` → **`2025-07`**.

Month-End Checklist used that id, so it showed:

`Period 2025-07 is still open for edits`

even when **no bank/cash rows exist in July 2025**. Unrelated to statement parse or cash-expense dates.

## Fix

`resolveMonthEndPeriodId(transactions, preferred)`:

1. Use `preferred` only if that month has ledger activity  
2. Else latest `YYYY-MM` that has activity  
3. Else calendar default month  

## Do

- Default Month-End to a month with bank/cash activity  
- Allow manual Period override in the UI  

## Do not

- Pass FY start month into Month-End lock when that month is empty  
- Treat empty July “still open” as a P&L error  
